            "review_title": "Review at Ringer Hut",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nSatisfying Jap comfort fast food, like competitor Sukiya\nAug 2019 • Family\nOne of the many new Japanese food chains to enter the fast-growing Vietnam F&B market, just like its rapidly expanding competitor, Sukiya. Both serve Jap comfort food in clean environments with consistent food standards - which is what Japan is well-known for. It's probably not known for gourmet food, but it's the kinda place that you know you can still find rather decent comfort food at decent prices for the family/self.\n\nWhile Sukiya is famous for its tender sliced beef rice, Ringer Hut is more famous for its Chinese-like Nagasaki noodles that comes with lots of ingredients like mixed vege, large shrimps, braised pork, fried chicken, onsen egg all in a bowl, giving it an overall more satisfying feels of a wholesome meal that's below 4usd!\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 19, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
