            "review_title": "Review at Ringer Hut",
            "review_text": "Yan Cui Travel\n253 contributions\n0\nThumbs up for Nagasaki Champon Restaurant\nSep 2019 • Solo\nWhile wandering around the downtown to find something for lunch, I got into this Japanese restaurant by chance (It's very close to Ben Thanh market). I was happily satisfied with the Champon soup with stewed egg, pork, shrimp and vege) and fried dumplings. Its Champon noodle is fatty and broth is tasty.\nI also felt relaxed while eating here thanks to the sentimental Japanese songs and the caring staff. (They actively fill up the water, clear off the table in a good and polite manner.)\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten September 23, 2019",
